evelop it um so and so  in this case um developing your  potential languages is the to the extent  to which you can really make it part of  your life and so  exactly you don't need to go to for  example when they say david speak to  spanish because you live in spain it's  not necessarily a concept but you know  living in spain doesn't make you a  fluent speaker you have to uh you have  to decide to make a  conscious effort to integrate not just  study the language but to make the  language part of your daily life because  people been living for 30 years in the  country they don't speak english and  there are people who live maybe six  months in a country and they go back to  their own country and they keep speaking  language native speakers mean because  they live with them or something else  happens well this is something i've  observed about you  um with languages because i notice in  one day you can switch between five six  seven different languages and it's um  it's not  something that you study it's not  something that you go to it's you know  it's part of your life and you know we  went to bars you know and it's just part  of your life where you just switch  between different languages and  you've developed a number of you know  deep relationships with different people  and so is this then also the trick to  you know maintaining all of these  languages as well because i think that  there are lots of people who think that  you have to study and study and study  for lots of time but but what is the  what's the truth you know how do you  live life with languages well the truth  is that um you know i  okay i work with languages i'm a  language coach so i work with languages  i use language  not teach how to learn but in the  language in a combination of languages  first i go out mostly with  borders even when i am in rome  so you know it's not a condition  you have to live in a foreign country  or i and i also live with  and obviously use languages on the  internet in general so that makes a huge  difference obviously  we have to consider the fact that we  have some strange sounds  well so the thing is that basically  it's  what makes a difference that i use  languages possibly on the internet in  real life in bars when i go out  with people i live and you know when you  live with somebody wake up and you have  an interesting conversation hey what did  you do yesterday or interesting  conversation in general what really  makes a difference  when you develop a certain level of  fluency is that on the one hand you  always have the same conversation how  you're doing et cetera et cetera but  when you develop that's that's what i  was talking about developing your human  potential because when you discover it's  also about connecting creating a strong  bond with people you really  and that motivates you pushes and pushes  you to have  to have interesting conversations  obviously the more interesting  conversations you have and the better  you can develop your vocabulary and your  expressions and you talk about different  topics and that's exactly what happened  it's not about the quantity of people  you know it's about the quality of  people you can stick to four or five uh  six interesting people i'm not counting  them it doesn't make any sense even one  can make a huge difference depending on  how but as i said before  we are all the sum of experiences in  people so the more people you talk to uh  the more  variety of actions and expressions you  have  sticking to some people as a core i  always like  absolutely and you know a comment that  or something i can say about you know  the way that you  speak spanish for example is you use  lots of different expressions and you  use words that  you will not find in any textbook you  know you only find  from  native speakers and so this is a result  because this is something i think that  surprises a lot of native speakers and  when people listen to you speaking in  languages and so this is a result of the  the depth to which you have you know  made connections with native speakers  and so this is just a snippet to uh  of a discussion that we are having for  my podcast which is the language is  culture podcast and so if you want to  find out more about you know this topic  about you know how we can make languages  part of our life how we can connect  language to culture and how this can  revolutionize you know the way that we  learn languages then make sure you come  over to languagesculture.com  and check that out um thank you for your  time today luca and we will catch you in  another video and in the podcast thank  you for watching ciao  you
 

